The function then iterates over the possible values of `i` and `j`, and for each value of `i`, it iterates over the possible values of `j`. If `i == j * x`, then `dp[j][i] = 1`, since there is only one way to partition `i` into `j` parts each of size `x`. Otherwise, for each value of `l` between `x` and `i`, it checks if `dp[j - 1][i - l] > 0`, which means that there is at least one way to partition `i - l` into `j - 1` parts each of size at least `x`. If this is the case, then `dp[j][i]` is incremented by the number of ways to partition `i - l` into `j - 1` parts, which is given by `dp[j - 1][i - l]`.

Finally, the function returns `dp[k][n]`, which represents the number of ways to partition `n` into `k` parts, each of size at least `x`.

